<title>GERMANY: Metro turns profit in first year.</title>
<headline>Metro turns profit in first year.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to end-December.</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			 717</p>
<p>    Group net profit less minorities   610</p>
<p>    Group DVFA profit			712</p>
<p>    Group income on ord. activities  1,062</p>
<p>    Group earnings per share	    7.10 marks</p>
<p>    Group sales inc. turnover tax   62,024</p>
<p>    Group net return on equity (pct   14.9</p>
<p>    Group Investment		     1,639</p>
<p>    Group DVFA cash flow		 1,898</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total		 20,777</p>
<p>    Equity capital			 4,826</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German retail group is Metro AG. The company, created out of a three-way merger last summer, did not publish comparative figures. It said it would propose a dividend of four marks on ordinary shares to its annual shareholders meeting and a payout of 4.25 marks on preferred shares.  </p>
<p>Metro also published the following breakdown of ordinary earnings in its business areas: (in millions of marks) @</p>
<p>    Metro wholesale			 420</p>
<p>    Department stores		     203</p>
<p>    Self-service stores		   100</p>
<p>    Food stores				61</p>
<p>    Electronics stores		    240</p>
<p>    Building supplies stores	    187</p>
<p>    Furniture stores		     -125</p>
<p>    Computer stores			  46</p>
<p>    Boutiques				  28</p>
<p>    Shoe shops				 25</p>
<p>    Mail order				 21</p>
<p>    Catering				   21</p>
<p>    Property				  179</p>
<p>    Others				     69 @</p>
<p>    Ord income before writedowns    1,475</p>
<p>    Holding company result	     -219</p>
<p>    Company writedowns		   -194</p>
<p>    Group ord. income		   1,062</p>
<p>    Taxes on income			 275</p>
<p>    Other taxes				70 @</p>
<p>    Group net profit			717</p>
<p>-- Douglas Busvine, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
